{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry about the Teams trouble. Please try these steps on your laptop: 1) In Teams, go to Settings, then Devices, and confirm the correct microphone, speaker, and camera are selected (if you use a dock or headset, check that its devices are chosen). 2) Check the physical mute key and camera privacy shutter, and close any other apps that might be using the camera, such as Zoom or a browser video call. 3) Use Teams' Make a test call to check audio. 4) Unplug and replug your headset or dock, then fully quit Teams (right-click its taskbar icon and choose Quit) and reopen it. 5) In Windows Settings, under Privacy & security, Camera and Microphone, make sure Teams is allowed. Please reply and let us know: does the problem continue after a full restart? Does the camera appear in Windows at all? Is the laptop you are using now BL-LT-0107? If the camera still doesn't work after these steps, we will escalate it for further hardware checks.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket EVAL-soft-01. Sofia Rossi (user 7, Marketing Coordinator, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00). Account active, not blocked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11. Only device on record is BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11 Pro, 54.7% disk free, no disk warning), but it is OFFLINE with no check-in for 12 days (last check-in 2026-09-29), which conflicts with her reporting a live Teams issue. Possibly she is on another machine or the device record is stale. Followed KB-025 quick checks and fixes via the reply. Not yet escalated: KB-025 escalation criteria (issue persists after restart, or Windows does not detect the camera) cannot be confirmed until the user replies. Tech: verify which device she is using and whether the inventory record for BL-LT-0107 is current.",
